silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_concrete_anchor_6#forbiddenshortcutsourcecell silm:hasLongDescription "The ForbiddenShortcutSourceCell is The second occurrence of GeneratedWitness in the lower row of the R4 diagram is the source of the dashed-red direct arrow. It is the same fixture (e.g., the GPT-drafted phrase \"Mittens is the colimit of its observable profile\") that appears in the upper row — but here its outgoing arrow attempts to bypass cite, type, and glue. The dashed-red rendering is the visual signal of forbidden-shortcut status; the lower-left cell exists in the diagram precisely to make this shortcut nameable and refusable. Without naming the forbidden route, the probe could not block it; without the lower cell, the probe diagram has no negative-regression target." .
